$WGS Earnings: Selling a 29% Implied Move

$WGS reports earnings Nov. 9. The Nov. 13 $65 straddle implies roughly a 29% move, based on its ~$19 midpoint and WGS at $65.33. That seems excessive to me.

Two earnings ago, WGS fell about 49% after a revenue miss and guidance cut. After its most recent earnings, it rose about 4.5% the next day, the currentimplied move is 29%! This makes no sense in my view. The reimbursement issue is much better understood now, and around $65 feels fair given the challenges. 

I’d sell this straddle with a limit order around $19 credit, sized appropriately. At expiration, that puts the breakevens near $46 and $84. I’d be happy to buy below $46, and I don’t think $WGS gets above $88.50 anytime soon. I think it’s great value.

